(a) The city commission may suspend, revoke, refuse to renew, or impose conditions of probation upon any license required under this chapter if:
(1) The license application is not filed in good faith or is filed by some person as subterfuge for any other person;
(2) Any applicant for a license or any licensee under this chapter willfully fails to comply with any provision of this chapter or with rules and regulations adopted by the city commission, or the Georgia Alcoholic Beverage Code;
(3) Any person to whom a license has been issued is no longer engaged in the sale of alcoholic beverages, malt beverages or wine or no longer qualifies as a licensee under this chapter;
